# TransformableImage

`TransformableImage` is the gesture layer behind image moving, zooming and rotating. It renders a `<div>`, listens for mouse drags, the wheel and one- or two-finger touch gestures on it, and turns each step into an `ImageTransform` (a move, a scale and a rotation) that it passes to `onTransform`. [`CropperBackgroundWrapper`](/docs/components/CropperBackgroundWrapper) is a thin adapter around it that forwards those transforms to the cropper.

```
CropperBackgroundWrapper
└─ TransformableImage            (div.advanced-cropper__background-wrapper)
   ├─ CropperBackgroundImage
   └─ stencil
```

Drags that start on the stencil never reach it: the stencil's [draggable parts](/docs/components/DraggableElement) stop those events first.

## Usage

Use it to build a custom `backgroundWrapperComponent`. The `onEvent` prop lets you inspect every native event before it is handled, and cancel the transform. This wrapper, for example, only zooms with the wheel while Ctrl (or ⌘) is held, and leaves plain wheel events to the page so it can scroll:

```svelte
<!-- CtrlWheelWrapper.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
	import type { Snippet } from 'svelte';
	import type { ClassValue } from 'svelte/elements';
	import {
		TransformableImage,
		isWheelEvent,
		type CropperRef,
		type TransformableImageEvent
	} from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	interface Props {
		cropper: CropperRef;
		class?: ClassValue;
		style?: string;
		disabled?: boolean;
		children?: Snippet;
	}

	let { cropper, class: className, style, disabled, children }: Props = $props();

	function onEvent(event: TransformableImageEvent, nativeEvent: Event) {
		if (isWheelEvent(nativeEvent) && !(nativeEvent.ctrlKey || nativeEvent.metaKey)) {
			// Skip the transform, and don't call preventDefault on the native event.
			event.preventDefault();
		} else {
			nativeEvent.preventDefault();
			nativeEvent.stopPropagation();
		}
	}
</script>

<TransformableImage
	class={className}
	{style}
	{onEvent}
	onTransform={cropper.transformImage}
	onTransformEnd={cropper.transformImageEnd}
	disabled={disabled || cropper.getTransitions().active}
>
	{@render children?.()}
</TransformableImage>
```

```svelte
<Cropper {src} backgroundWrapperComponent={CtrlWheelWrapper} />
```

## Props

| Prop             | Type                                                                                | Default | Description                                                                                                                              |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `onTransform`    | <code>(transform: ImageTransform) =&gt; void</code>                                 | —       | Called for each gesture step with the transform to apply.                                                                                |
| `onTransformEnd` | `() => void`                                                                        | —       | Called once when a gesture ends: on mouse up, when the last finger lifts, or `timeout` milliseconds after the last wheel event.          |
| `onEvent`        | <code>(event: TransformableImageEvent, nativeEvent: Event) =&gt; unknown</code>     | —       | Called with every native event the component handles, before it acts on it. See below.                                                  |
| `mouseMove`      | `boolean`                                                                           | `true`  | Move the image by dragging it with the mouse.                                                                                            |
| `touchMove`      | `boolean`                                                                           | `true`  | Move the image with one finger.                                                                                                          |
| `touchScale`     | `boolean`                                                                           | `true`  | Zoom with a two-finger pinch.                                                                                                            |
| `touchRotate`    | `boolean`                                                                           | `false` | Rotate with two fingers.                                                                                                                 |
| `wheelScale`     | `boolean` \| `{ ratio: number }`                                                     | `true`  | Zoom with the wheel. `ratio` is the zoom step per wheel event, and `true` means `0.1`.                                                   |
| `timeout`        | `number`                                                                            | `500`   | How long after the last wheel event the wheel gesture ends. Read once, when the component mounts.                                        |
| `disabled`       | `boolean`                                                                           | —       | Stops producing transforms. Events are still handled (and prevented, unless `preventDefault` is off).                                     |
| `preventDefault` | `boolean`                                                                           | `true`  | Call `preventDefault()` and `stopPropagation()` on handled events, so the page doesn't scroll or zoom. Ignored when `onEvent` is set.      |
| `class`          | `ClassValue`                                                                        | —       | Classes for the element. Upstream's `className`.                                                                                         |
| `style`          | `string`                                                                            | —       | Inline style for the element.                                                                                                            |
| `children`       | `Snippet`                                                                           | —       | The content: the background and the stencil.                                                                                             |

## `TransformableImageEvent`

`onEvent` receives an instance of this exported class for each native event:

| Member             | Type         | Description                                                                         |
| ------------------ | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `active`           | `boolean`    | `true` when a gesture is already in progress.                                       |
| `defaultPrevented` | `boolean`    | `true` after `preventDefault()` was called.                                         |
| `preventDefault()` | `() => void` | Cancels the transform for this event. It doesn't touch the native event.            |

<Admonition type="warning" title="onEvent replaces the default handling">

When `onEvent` is set, the component no longer prevents the native events itself. Call `nativeEvent.preventDefault()` and `nativeEvent.stopPropagation()` in your handler for the events you keep, as the example above does, or the page will scroll and zoom along with the image.

</Admonition>

## Event handling

The component listens with native, non-passive listeners: `mousedown`, `touchstart` and `wheel` on its element, and `mousemove`, `mouseup`, `touchmove` and `touchend` on `window`. Non-passive listeners are what allow it to prevent page scrolling during touch gestures, which Svelte's `on*` attributes can't do for touch events. Only touches that start inside the element take part in a gesture.

## CSS classes

The component has no class of its own. Its element carries the `class` it receives: with the default cropper that is `advanced-cropper__background-wrapper`.
